    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Question\n\nI have looked through the documentation and can't find any reference to removing specific bindings to get picked up by clue. \r\nBindings such as <leader><leader> are getting automatically added. \r\nIs there anyway for me to remove these? \r\nFor example, for whichkey there is a whichkey_ignore that you can use for this purpose. \r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.clue</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have looked through the documentation and can't find any reference to removing specific bindings to get picked up by clue.<br>\nBindings such as  are getting automatically added.<br>\nIs there anyway for me to remove these?<br>\nFor example, for whichkey there is a whichkey_ignore that you can use for this purpose.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.clue\nQuestion\nI have looked through the documentation and can't find any reference to removing specific bindings to get picked up by clue.\nBindings such as  are getting automatically added.\nIs there anyway for me to remove these?\nFor example, for whichkey there is a whichkey_ignore that you can use for this purpose.\nThanks!",
